<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adelaide del Vasto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1075–<a href="/years/1118">1118</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-countess-of-vermandois">Adelaide</a> del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasto">Vasto</a> was the third wife of Roger I, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, and regent of the County of Sicily for her young sons from 1101 to 1112. She moved the court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> and prepared the way for her son Roger II, later the first King of Sicily. In 1113 she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem">Baldwin I of Jerusalem</a>, but the match was annulled and she returned to Sicily.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adelaide-del-vasto.jpg" alt="Adelaide del Vasto" width="158" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maître de Fauvel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:R%C3%A9pudiation_d%27Ad%C3%A9la%C3%AFde_de_Montferrat.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
